From 1ce5893416b5ed6c223a69202b0a022b3006dd2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 16:33:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05799/11362] [outer-loop] broaden blocked_* verdict exemption
 to trust the verdict prefix directly

User asked to dig into a new .482 flag: exp5274 (solver-grounded
constraint extraction retry, gated) correctly checked its own
preconditions, found llama_cpp_gpu_offload_unavailable, and wrote an
honest blocked_preconditions verdict without attempting any inference --
extraction_results=[], rows_total=0, exactly the Pre-Launch Preconditions
Discipline's intended behavior. It still got flagged DURATION_TOO_SHORT
(duration_s=0.14).

Unlike the five prior fixes this week (all "legitimate small workload,
no substrate category recognized it"), this is a different root cause:
a pre-existing exemption (_is_precondition_check_only_blocked) already
existed for exactly this case, but required the artifact to ALSO declare
inference_substrate=="precondition_check_only" specifically. exp5274's
script hardcodes the same INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE constant
(live_llm_inference_local_gguf_sota) on both its live and blocked
branches -- a design choice that means the substrate string alone can't
distinguish "ran for real" from "blocked before touching the GPU."

Fix: broadened _is_precondition_check_only_blocked to trust a bare
blocked_*-prefixed honest_verdict on its own, per this project's own
Verdict Terminal-Prefix Discipline + Pre-Launch Preconditions Discipline
-- a blocked_* verdict is already a mandated, structured admission that
the compute-bound work did not happen; requiring one specific substrate
string in addition was over-narrow. Verified both existing call sites
(duration_floor_for_artifact, check_duration_vs_claim) are duration-
related only, so this doesn't weaken the tautology, methodology, or gate
checks. Also extended check_methodology_present with the same exemption
-- a genuinely blocked artifact has nothing to seed or checksum either.

7 new tests (tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_blocked_verdict_
duration_exemption.py): recognition-function coverage (bare blocked_
prefix alone is sufficient; explicit precondition_check_only substrate
still works; a non-blocked verdict is NOT exempted), an exact exp5274
reproduction now clean, a duration-floor-is-None guard, and a regression
guard confirming a non-blocked artifact sharing the same substrate string
still needs its real floor (the exemption is verdict-gated, not
substrate-string-gated). Full suite (284 tests) green. Corpus-wide
dry-run sanity check stable (~5 qualifying artifacts, normal drift, no
new flood).

Un-quarantined exp5274: 0 flags (was 1 CRITICAL + 1 WARN). Its own test
suite (5 tests) still passes after patching.

